### FKs
> ERROR:  insert or update on table "albums_assets_assets" violates foreign key constraint

Yeah, kind of expected, not good, not too bad. 
This happened in a sibling issue https://github.com/immich-app/immich/discussions/20328#discussioncomment-13941899 as well while recreating FKs: "Encountered several errors due to dangling foreign keys".
Reason: while FKs were missing, if you remove an album, it removes a record in `album`, but corresponding auxillary records in `album_assets` are not removed and become dangling. Now, when adding FKs back, those dangling records in `album_assets` cannot find their corresponding `album` record.

Therefore we have to do some cleanup by removing dangling records.

Cleanup of dangling records and creation of FKs in a single transaction:
```sql
begin; 

DELETE FROM albums_assets_assets aa
WHERE NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM public.assets a WHERE a.id = aa."assetsId" )
   OR NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM public.albums al WHERE al.id = aa."albumsId" );

DELETE FROM public.asset_files af
WHERE NOT EXISTS ( SELECT 1 FROM public.assets a WHERE a.id = af."assetId" );

ALTER TABLE albums_assets_assets ADD CONSTRAINT "FK_4bd1303d199f4e72ccdf998c621" FOREIGN KEY ("assetsId") REFERENCES public.assets(id) ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE CASCADE;
ALTER TABLE asset_files ADD CONSTRAINT "FK_e3e103a5f1d8bc8402999286040" FOREIGN KEY ("assetId") REFERENCES public.assets(id) ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE CASCADE;
ALTER TABLE albums_assets_assets ADD CONSTRAINT "FK_e590fa396c6898fcd4a50e40927" FOREIGN KEY ("albumsId") REFERENCES public.albums(id) ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE CASCADE;

-- if outcome looks good
commit;
```

