@mertalev The reindex is triggered by the condition in the provided code snippet: [this](https://github.com/immich-app/immich/blob/61a9d5cbc7c3f3ba58cb6b22e5fb60f2800180e8/server/src/repositories/database.repository.ts#L209). When the total number of vector records exceeds 4,194,304, this script recreates and re-balances the index from 4,096 to 8,192 slices. Currently, this process occurs during server boot and can take several hours, depending on the disk I/O and CPU resources.

In my experience, when the transaction fails, the `face_index` and `clip_index` are gone. Consequently, the app becomes unresponsive while searching photos, as it starts looping through millions of records.

I believe we are making a trade-off between minimizing the disk space occupied by reindexing vector indexes and ensuring the app remains usable even when the indexes need to be rebuilt. For my personal use case, we have ample disk space for the database, so I don’t want the app to become unusable for hours.

